  "known_local_policies": [
    "Rolling Fireball partitions one source-adjusted budget by current Health along one direction on the original board. Choose left/right once only when both physical sides exist; illegal Dormant or Location/interactable slots stop propagation, following official patch 27.6. No deathrattle-created recipient joins the original simultaneous batch.",
    "Combustion deals its full source-adjusted amount to the original target, and max(0,budget-original Health) independently to each original immediate legal neighbor. Neither immunity/Divine Shield nor recipient multipliers recalculate this excess. One budget includes Spell Damage once; original tag 349 is preserved as source data, not interpreted as whole-spell immunity.",
    "Blast Wave uses original SPELL HealthResult Overkill conditions: own turn, actual damage greater than positive original Health, no prevention or previously doomed target. Each actual original result generates one random Mage spell from the ordinary full source domain. Original callbacks and reward timing are local policy pending CN edge calibration.",
    "Ignite native growing base damage is explicitly deferred to the next incremental implementation, not treated as a supported blank spell.",
    "Version/hotfix alignment and CN edge calibration remain deferred; no source membership is cropped by implementation coverage."
  ],
